./LOGBOOK.md:641:- ACTIVITY: New associations and socketless reservations retain one bounded initial idle lifetime, but `Reserve`, `EnsureFamilies`, and `EnsureTokenFamilies` no longer touch an existing incarnation. The registry rearms activity only when the serialized socket callback reports a successful outbound send or received datagram. Deterministic injected-clock tests assert exact deadlines and physical timer-arm epochs across numeric and resolved-domain IPv4-to-IPv6 family attachment: success refreshes once; `EAGAIN`, `ENOBUFS`, resolver failure, caller cancellation, and terminal socket errors do not refresh before survival or cleanup.
