./LOGBOOK.md:772:### 0535 — Host VPN production start errors are normalized at both Apple seams (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
./LOGBOOK.md:773:- FIX: Both iOS and macOS `VPNHostSession` adapters now catch synchronous `NETunnelProviderSession.startTunnel(options:)` errors and translate them through the existing `VPNPreferencePlatformError` model before crossing into `VPNSessionController`. Public `NEVPNError.configurationInvalid`, `.configurationDisabled`, and `.connectionFailed` retain their stable results; every other `NSError` retains its original domain and integer code.
./LOGBOOK.md:774:- INTEGRATION: A freshly loaded exact-owned but disabled manager correctly failed inside `OwnedVPNManagerRepository`, but the controller initially leaked the repository error type. The start preflight now normalizes that one repository result to `VPNSessionControllerError.configurationDisabled` without invoking the system start API or duplicating ownership logic.
./LOGBOOK.md:778:### 0526 — Host VPN controller review requests production error-translation rework (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
./LOGBOOK.md:780:- REGRESSION: `IOSVPNHostSession.startTunnel` and `MacOSVPNHostSession.startTunnel` forward the public `NETunnelProviderSession.startTunnel(options:)` thrown `NSError` unchanged, while `VPNSessionController.performStart` maps only `VPNPreferencePlatformError` / `VPNPlatformError` and otherwise erases the real domain/code to reflected type plus code 0. The unit test injects a pre-normalized fake error, so the production adapter path is untested and cannot satisfy the accepted exact synchronous `NEVPNError` mapping.
./LOGBOOK.md:783:### 0511 — Host VPN control keeps system and provider authorities independent (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
./LOGBOOK.md:784:- DECISION: `OwnedVPNManagerRepository` remains the only ownership/schema authority and now hands out a session only from a freshly loaded exact-owned current manager. `VPNSessionController` retains no manager cache or forwarding state; iOS/macOS wrappers retain the fresh manager only to keep its exact public `NETunnelProviderSession` alive for the command/observer lifetime.
./LOGBOOK.md:787:- ERROR CONTRACT: All 19 public `NEVPNConnectionError` codes, provider codes 1001–1009, unknown domains/codes, provider unknown codes, nil errors, and timeout/cancellation unavailability map to stable finite reasons while system status remains authoritative.
./LOGBOOK.md:790:### 0442 — Apple VPN terminal observation registers before authoritative status (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
./LOGBOOK.md:791:- REGRESSION: Both NetworkExtension adapters read `NEVPNConnection.status` before installing `NEVPNStatusDidChange`, so a terminal transition in that gap could be lost and an already-stopped session could falsely reach the 15-second `stopTimedOut` path.
./LOGBOOK.md:796:### 0421 — VPN preference operations are non-reentrant and NSNumber versions are exact (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
./LOGBOOK.md:802:### 0405 — VPN manager rework preserves all future versions and fresh authority (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
./LOGBOOK.md:808:### 0351 — Owned VPN preferences are shared policy with thin platform clients (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
./LOGBOOK.md:810:- SAFETY: Ensure never enables; the explicit enable result names the OS-level possibility that another enterprise VPN is disabled. Duplicate repair removes every freshly revalidated current-schema inactive exact-owned manager, reloads after each removal, proves zero, then recreates one. Unmarked, unrelated, wrong-type, corrupt duplicate, active duplicate, and future-owned managers are zero-write paths.
./LOGBOOK.md:811:- IDENTITY: The complete host/provider/App Group/Keychain `PlatformVPNIdentity` remains injectable for deterministic fixtures. Both production factories fail closed until `TASK-260715-ypo7yo` supplies accepted signed bindings; no guessed identifier landed.
./LOGBOOK.md:818:- SCHEMA: Provider stop metadata extends diagnostics v1 to 97 counters, 57 gauges, and 11 finite error codes across the same 10 domains. The schema still retains no endpoints, DNS names, traffic identifiers, secrets, configuration, localized errors, or free-form labels.
./LOGBOOK.md:819:- COVERAGE: Shared tests run through iOS and macOS seams for all four commands, hostile/oversized/future/mutating inputs, duplicates, nil handlers, retirement, all raw Apple reasons, startup and cleanup deadlines, stop-wins-start, fatal handoff, deallocation, and two 100-cycle baselines. Existing coordinator tests retain every startup acquisition/cancellation point and route-clear uncertainty coverage.
./LOGBOOK.md:821:### 0245 — VPN lifecycle separates ownership, enablement, system state, and runtime capability (TASK-260715-1q4qhw)
./LOGBOOK.md:823:- PLATFORM FINDING: Apple limits `loadAllFromPreferences` to configurations created by the calling app, but enabling an enterprise VPN can cause the OS to disable another app's enterprise VPN. Therefore ordinary ensure preserves/creates a disabled configuration and explicit foreground user intent owns enable/save/reload. Relux never mutates the unrelated manager object and reports the system-level enable effect truthfully.
./LOGBOOK.md:828:- DECISION: Fault injection uses the coordinator's injected cancellation-check seam to fail at fourteen exact before/after ownership boundaries. This keeps production code unchanged while proving reverse rollback, one disconnecting publication, one terminal publication, exact error mapping, and single cleanup for configuration, SSH, TCP, DNS, packet plane, settings, and packet-read ownership.
./LOGBOOK.md:829:- COVERAGE: The explicit control table covers rejected duplicate starts, idempotent stops, healthy/stale/late callbacks in usable, stopping, disconnected, and failed states; phase gates now include configuration as well as SSH, TCP, DNS, packet preparation, settings apply, packet activation, and final health. All four mandatory dependency failures must revoke capability before cleanup begins.
./LOGBOOK.md:843:- COVERAGE: A package-internal async handoff hook, following the existing core test-hook pattern, deterministically injects current-generation DNS health loss after child completion and independently pauses the same boundary for caller cancellation. Neither test issues a masking `stop()`; both assert no capability revival, exactly-once reverse cleanup, a zero external resource ledger, and the coordinator baseline footprint.
./LOGBOOK.md:848:- SAFETY: Settings are requested only after validated configuration, authenticated SSH, TCP readiness, SSH-only safe DNS readiness, pure packet-plane preparation, and mandatory health checks. Unknown apply failures are conservatively treated as an uncertain commit and cleared; definite non-commit skips clear. A clear failure publishes TCP/DNS false while truthfully retaining `routesInstalled=true` and `routeState=clearFailed`.
./LOGBOOK.md:849:- CLEANUP: Teardown closes admission, stops packet reads/native work, clears settings when required, then stops DNS, TCP, and SSH in reverse acquisition order. The coordinator releases configuration references and all tracked task/resource handles; repeated stop calls join the same cleanup.
./LOGBOOK.md:860:- DECISION: `RuntimeDiagnosticsStore` owns one bounded generation with 96 counters, 56 gauges, one cumulative DNS-latency histogram, and at most one cataloged error per each of 10 finite domains. Packet/HEV use its `TunnelMetrics` recorder, SSH uses the same recorder without lane identity, and coordinator/TCP/DNS/route/memory use typed finite-category updates; unknown free-form metric names are counted then discarded without retaining the label.
./LOGBOOK.md:862:- PRIVACY: The default schema has no lane/run/flow IDs, DNS or destination fields, addresses, credentials, commands/stdin, payload content, or traffic samples. State transition times are monotonic process-uptime milliseconds; errors retain only validated domain/code; flow, memory, route, health, packet/byte, drop-reason, DNS-result, and SSH values are aggregates.
./LOGBOOK.md:869:- SAFETY: A future lifecycle `routeState` previously decoded as `unknown` while preserving true TCP, safe-DNS, route-installed, and health facts. Route state now participates in the shared fail-safe projection for both decoded and directly constructed lifecycle snapshots, forcing every capability false when it is unknown.
./LOGBOOK.md:876:- CAPABILITY: TCP, safe DNS, UDP, route mode, route-installed state, and health are independent required facts with no full-mode bit. Unknown output lifecycle/route values project to `unknown` with every capability false; generation/sequence ordering rejects lower generations and non-increasing snapshots.
./LOGBOOK.md:880:- DECISION: The packet-tunnel extension owns one actor-serialized runtime generation, with immutable app-message snapshots and no live forwarding dependency on the containing app. Startup is configuration -> verified/authenticated SSH -> TCP/DNS readiness -> pure packet preflight -> settings apply -> existing PacketBridge.start/read activation -> TCP + safe-DNS publication; every failure rolls back through one idempotent, non-cancellable stopping path.
./LOGBOOK.md:881:- OWNERSHIP: M1PacketPlaneSession is the sole owner of the HEV private SOCKS boundary and dispatches authenticated CONNECT to TCP plus only approved virtual-DNS UDP/TCP to DNS; other UDP is rejected until M2. The coordinator proceeds against fakes independently of production factories, and both branches converge at TASK-260715-30ugfm.
./LOGBOOK.md:883:- SAFETY: Settings clear is called only after a committed or uncertain apply. A required failed/uncertain clear publishes capabilities false but truthfully retains routesInstalled=true with routeState=clearFailed; a clear that was unnecessary or confirmed publishes routesInstalled=false. Legacy version protocol v1 remains byte-exact while new M1 commands/snapshots use explicit schemas.
./LOGBOOK.md:884:- REVIEW: Independent agent review requested and verified corrections across ownership, source-interface feasibility, versions, dependencies, transitions, and route cleanup, then accepted all five AC. PlantUML is unavailable and local Graphviz is broken by missing libltdl; authoritative sources and the toolchain anomaly are attached rather than claiming rendered evidence.
./LOGBOOK.md:907:- DECISION: The codec preserves HEV domain bytes as an opaque 1–248-byte wire value, including non-ASCII and NUL. DNS presentation-form, invalid A-label, raw-IP-text, and IDNA policy remains exclusively in the later Go resolution gate; neither codec normalizes, resolves, or logs domain bytes. The endpoint type is direction-neutral so a response encodes the relay-observed source rather than substituting the original destination.
./LOGBOOK.md:912:- IMPLEMENTATION: Swift and Go now encode the four-byte big-endian body length plus type/flags/association ID as separate header/payload write slices, and decode arbitrary partial/coalesced stream reads while retaining at most one negotiated frame plus the fixed prefix. Prefix bounds are checked before the first body allocation; generated message metadata drives direction, association-ID, fixed-payload, reserved-flag, and negotiated DNS-priority validation.
./LOGBOOK.md:945:- FINDING: Pinned HEV caps UDP-in-TCP copy buffers at `UDP_BUF_SIZE = 1500` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:26`); `recvmmsg_tcp` returns `-1` (stream-fatal, not a drop) when `datlen > 1500 − addrlen` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:203-206`). With ADR-020 keeping HEV unmodified, the relay→client reply path physically cannot carry a UDP payload above 1481 bytes (IPv6). This, plus unfragmented 1500-MTU egress, fixes `maxUDPPayload = 1472` as a v1 wire constant; raising it is an HEV-fork decision, not a protocol negotiation.
./LOGBOOK.md:946:- DECISION: Baselines (all injectable, schema-owned floors/hard ceilings, fail-closed on out-of-range config): maxFrame [2048,65536] advertise 4096; maxAssociations 256 [1,1024]; per-assoc queue client 32KiB/relay 64KiB; aggregate/direction client 1MiB/relay 4MiB; control reserve 16/64KiB; DNS WRR 4:1; idle client 60s / relay 120s (RFC 4787 REQ-5 floor; client-first stagger shrinks crossed-expiry reopen race). `0x0005` split into violation (>1472, association-fatal) vs policy (lowered local cap, drop); `0x0006` edge-triggered per saturation episode.
./LOGBOOK.md:954:- NOTE: 248-byte domain wire cap (inherited HEV one-byte `HDRLEN`) is below the 253-byte DNS presentation maximum; TASK-260715-1q7u14 should include a boundary vector. Review evidence: board outcome `TASK-260715-111tde_review.md`.
./LOGBOOK.md:959:- DECISION: Build identity uses a separate bounded `relux-relay --identity --protocol 1` exec record matched to the signed manifest before `--stdio --protocol 1`; the fixed 12/16-byte v1 hello remains unchanged and framed stdout stays uncontaminated. DNS priority is a negotiated scheduling hint only. HEV `MSGLEN` is DATA length, `HDRLEN` includes the three-byte prefix, and domain wire length is capped at 248 by one-byte `HDRLEN`.
./LOGBOOK.md:980:- MILESTONE: BUG-260720-2zh86a accepted → done. `make validate-native` full Apple matrix no longer stops on the HEV/libssh2 deployment-target mismatch; packet-plane Apple builds and physical validation (12x6oq) unblocked on this axis.
